{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2d","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn with its vertices on the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf1e5a1f898db422b11eb7246758290046d9386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJ = PK = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498d2203eeef25f0a4a2a64d57e8462925343e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JQ = KR = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf714d449b9c6ffe450fdbb57763660b3ee8f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> m, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1e54de87ff17f00d801c9de48ffd0dc0b15494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> m, as shown\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2d&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 2 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the fraction of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> that is covered by rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use solutions from previous parts or the Pythagorean theorem to show that the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> drawn from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87baf8c593baa599ca7989d2a1ff6a760720b26c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa0b7fed66d008bcfc07d3baa7d71c801d7adcd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31dd37806f1902cbe5f8e8fe65561aef37de6d12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{44 \\times 66}{2} = 22 \\times 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e134066861513d827b5750f9e4e6a7a47bfcfee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Next, from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">part b</a> and known lengths, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d76a000f5c0127cc2b134d00d4ee6cfb542697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML = 6 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a29ddcc54d2cd8d638f00d8af4dba67b9c09ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = 40 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. The area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8ce6f9bd49ed1fad907807d65c636eea1275a378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e134066861513d827b5750f9e4e6a7a47bfcfee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the fraction of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> covered by rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd1a380cbe1f2ffaf372b7595e8a13dabb618b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6 \\times 40}{22 \\times 66} = \\frac{20}{11 \\times 11} = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{121}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"218\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012745\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 95/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1099/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4469/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.564      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   13.564      1 -total\n 39.01%    5.291      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36893:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012745 and revision id 285648. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}